;;; integral-convergence.scm -- MEASURABLE FUNCTIONS CLOSED UNDER +, *, sup and
;;; lim inf; APPROXIMATION BY SIMPLE FUNCTIONS; MONOTONE CONVERGENCE; ADDITIVITY
;;; OF THE INTEGRAL; FATOU'S LEMMA; DOMINATED CONVERGENCE.  Agent M-3 of the October roadmap (week 3,
;;; scratchpad/triage/WEEK3.md).  Helper prefix icv-.  Every theorem `modulo 0'.
;;;
;;; THE SUPPORTS OF structure-library/integral.scm PROVEN HERE (same statements,
;;; copied as S-expressions; the band prints "re-installing the same statement"):
;;;   measurable-fn-sup, measurable-fn-liminf, measurable-fn-eplus,
;;;   measurable-fn-etimes, integral-simple-approx, monotone-convergence,
;;;   integral-additive, fatou, dominated-convergence (all nine).
;;;
;;; THE ROUTE.
;;;  (A) order in [0,+inf]: totality, lt/le transitivity, the two faces of
;;;      a < ESUP(S) (esup-lt-witness, esup-gt-of-member).
;;;  (B) IS-MEASURABLE-FN is the tail criterion; for alpha < 0 the tail is omega,
;;;      so nonnegative alpha suffice (measurable-fn-of-nonneg-tails); then
;;;      { alpha < sup_n f_n } = U_n { alpha < f_n } (measurable-fn-sup-of-values).
;;;  (C) { alpha < inf_{p in D} f_p } = U_k { x : forall p in D. alpha + 1/(k+1) <= f_p(x) },
;;;      the inner set the complement of a countable union of guarded tails
;;;      (measurable-fn-inf-of-values); the lower limit is the supremum of the
;;;      tail infima (measurable-fn-liminf).
;;;  (D) the grid k/(n+1) indexed by NN x NN: a floor (rr-nn-floor-mul, by
;;;      nn-least-element) and a grid point between two reals (rr-grid-between).
;;;      The asserted qq-dense-in-rr is NOT used.
;;;  (E),(F) { alpha < f + g } and { alpha < f g } as countable unions of grid
;;;      cells; the real arithmetic of the product (rr-lt-div-of-lt-mul,
;;;      rr-recip-swap-lt, rr-lt-mul-of-grid).
;;;  (G) sums against suprema: sup u + sup v <= L when u(n) + v(n) <= L for
;;;      nondecreasing u, v (esup-eplus-le); the finite-sum form by finite-set
;;;      induction (rps-finsum-esup-le).
;;;  (H) a function factored through a finite measurable partition is simple
;;;      (simple-fn-of-partition).
;;;  (I) c u <= L for every c in (0,1) gives u <= L (rps-le-of-scaled);
;;;      w sup m <= sup (w m) (esup-etimes-ge).
;;;  (J) c s restricted to a set B: simple, with simple integral
;;;      SUM_y (c y) mu({s = y} n B) (simple-restrict-integral, by
;;;      simple-integral-partition with KS = s(omega) u {+inf}).
;;;  (K),(L) MONOTONE CONVERGENCE (Rudin 1.26): for simple s <= sup f_n and
;;;      0 < c < 1 the sets E_n = { c s <= f_n } increase to omega on every
;;;      level set, continuity from below and (G) give
;;;      c SIMPLE-INTEGRAL(s) <= sup_n INTEGRAL(f_n) (mct-simple-below).
;;;  (M) FATOU from monotone convergence on the tail infima.
;;;  (N) APPROXIMATION (Rudin 1.17) by the dyadic staircase in ESUP form,
;;;      s_n(x) = ESUP { k 2^-n : k 2^-n <= f(x), k 2^-n <= n }
;;;      (esup-grid-max, grid-staircase-value, grid-staircase-simple).
;;;  (O) ADDITIVITY from (N), monotone convergence three times and
;;;      simple-integral-additive (esup-eplus-eq, simple-fn-eplus).
;;;  (P),(Q) bricks for dominated convergence: { v < u } measurable
;;;      (measurable-fn-lt-set), constants, the finite part { u in RR }, a
;;;      function of finite integral is finite a.e. (integral-finite-null),
;;;      integrals are blind to null sets (integral-le-off-null), the
;;;      difference g - f (0 where g = +inf) is measurable and
;;;      INTEGRAL(g - f) + INTEGRAL(f) = INTEGRAL(g) (measurable-fn-sub, integral-sub).
;;;  (R) lim inf <= lim sup, bounds pass to lim sup, and the reflection
;;;      lim inf (c - a_n) = c - lim sup a_n (eliminf-reflection).
;;;  (S) DOMINATED CONVERGENCE: Fatou on f_n and on g - f_n.  NOTE: the notes'
;;;      proof of Prop. 2.28 (p. 18) bounds INTEGRAL(h_k) <= INTEGRAL(f_k) <= INTEGRAL(f),
;;;      but f_k <= f is not given; the upper bound needs the second Fatou
;;;      (Rudin 1.34's argument), which is the one followed here.
;;;
;;; LOAD WINDOW.  lo: the latest citations are those of
;;; theorem-library/integral-laws (load.scm line 3384: integral-in,
;;; integral-monotone, integral-simple, integral-unfold, simple-integral-*,
;;; measurable-fn-ge, measurable-fn-level-set, finsum-cm-*, rps-finsum-*,
;;; sigma-algebra-preimage-finite-in, etimes-*) and theorem-library/measure-laws
;;; (3383: measure-continuity-from-below, measure-monotone); einf-* (limsup-tests,
;;; 3381).  No late tactic (no contra, prep, ineq-supply); the kit procedures used
;;; (dk-crs-opaque!, dk-fun-ext!, dk-nn!, dk-case-if!, dk-if-branch!) are in
;;; driver-kit.scm.  hi: nothing in the tree cites the eight names (grep
;;; "'monotone-convergence" finds only monotone-convergence-rr).  Slot:
;;; immediately after "theorem-library/integral-laws".
